From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 23:35:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ci): separate completion gates from live-comment pollers
 [daveey]

---
diff --git a/.github/FAST-LANE.md b/.github/FAST-LANE.md
index e901a297c52ae4dd596336fffee3548b81d5e51d..bc70deebbf2a65a69f6fffad762709b2b04808ff 100644
--- a/.github/FAST-LANE.md
+++ b/.github/FAST-LANE.md
@@ -5,8 +5,10 @@
 `hermes-hub`, Docker `docker-ci`, or long-lived observer `hermes-hub-poll` lanes.
 Jobs keep their existing names, conditions, dependencies, steps, permissions,
 timeouts and required-result semantics. In particular, neither heavy tests nor
-the advisory full-tree `ruff + ty diff` moves here. Existing aggregators stay on
-the poll lane; no checks are added to that lane.
+the advisory full-tree `ruff + ty diff` moves here. Completion aggregates and the
+CI timing report use the general `hermes-hub` lane, never the observer-only pool:
+long-running live-comment pollers can await those very jobs and occupy every slot.
+The `!cancelled()` condition still keeps superseded runs from latching their group.
 
 ## Evidence behind admission
 
diff --git a/scripts/fork-ci-runner.sh b/scripts/fork-ci-runner.sh
index f3a27d7e4865eeee47f268f3dcf5cb5464d54370..4f29a1c3eec835ed62771063a109dd413e074792 100755
--- a/scripts/fork-ci-runner.sh
+++ b/scripts/fork-ci-runner.sh
@@ -23,12 +23,10 @@ rm -f ./*.bak
 sed -i.bak -E 's/^([[:space:]]*runs-on:[[:space:]]*)(\[self-hosted, hermes-hub\]|ubuntu-latest|ubuntu-24\.04)[[:space:]]*$/\1[self-hosted, hermes-hub-poll]/' ci-review-comment.yml
 rm -f ./*.bak
 
-# Aggregator/report jobs (cheap: checkout + a python script) go to the poll
-# runners and skip on cancellation. With `if: always()` on a [hermes-hub] test
-# runner, a CANCELLED run (superseded PR head) still waited for a busy heavy
-# runner to run its aggregator, held the ci-<PR> concurrency group, and left
-# the new head's run `pending` (PR #53, PR #50). `!cancelled()` keeps
-# failure/skip reporting; a cancelled run now completes at once.
+# Aggregator/report jobs use general capacity, never the observer-only pool:
+# live-comment pollers can await these jobs and fill every poll slot (PR #221).
+# Keep cancellation skipping: a CANCELLED run's always() gate used to hold
+# its concurrency group while queued (PR #53, PR #50).
 # Detect gets 5 min: a 1-min cap was cancelling whole runs on a loaded hub
 # (checkout 52s + compare-API retry), which skipped every lane.
 python3 - <<'PY'
@@ -44,7 +42,7 @@ for f, names in JOBS.items():
         assert m, (f, name)
         block = m.group(0)
         new = re.sub(r'(?m)^(    if: )always\(\)$', r"\1${{ !cancelled() }}", block)
-        new = re.sub(r'(?m)^(    runs-on: )\[self-hosted, hermes-hub\]$', r'\1[self-hosted, hermes-hub-poll]', new)
+        new = re.sub(r'(?m)^(    runs-on: )\[self-hosted, hermes-hub(?:-poll)?\]$', r'\1[self-hosted, hermes-hub]', new)
         t = t.replace(block, new)
     if f == 'ci.yaml':
         t = re.sub(r"(  detect:\n    name: Detect affected areas\n    runs-on: [^\n]*\n    timeout-minutes: )1\n",
diff --git a/tests/ci/test_fast_runner_routing.py b/tests/ci/test_fast_runner_routing.py
index 5bc80ad7da3c7748bee11df2e81cecb1e153a047..07fec688aa55b06967dba75d59d41886ed9219d6 100644
--- a/tests/ci/test_fast_runner_routing.py
